{{#extend "layout" showSource=true}}

  {{#content "main"}}
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Recipe &middot; dynamic partials</p>
    <h1>When the partial name is undefined</h1>
    <p>
      A dynamic partial takes its name from the model:
      <code>&#123;&#123;&gt; (lookup this 'partial')&#125;&#125;</code>. When the key is missing
      from one record out of many, v1 rendered an empty string and carried on. v2 fails the
      page — so guard the call, and let the warning tell you which key went missing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="grid">
    {{#each model.blocks}}
    <article class="card">
      <h3>{{label}}</h3>
      {{#if partial}}
      {{> (lookup this "partial")}}
      {{else}}
      <p class="tone-warn">
        This record carries no <code>partial</code> key. The guard kept the page; the console
        line <code>lookup: 'partial' is undefined in dynamic-partials.hbs</code> names the key
        and the view, which is the diagnostic v1 never gave you.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">Looked up anyway, to produce that warning: &ldquo;{{lookup this "partial"}}&rdquo;</p>
      {{/if}}
    </article>
    {{/each}}
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <h2>Why this one bites</h2>
    <p>
      In a real migration this was 40 pages of one site failing with
      <code>The partial undefined could not be found</code> — a message naming neither the key
      nor the page. The same 40 pages had been shipping <em>without</em> that block under v1,
      green, for a year. v2 is right to fail, and the warning is there so the diagnosis takes a
      second rather than an afternoon.
    </p>
  </div>
  {{/content}}

  {{#content "demo"}}
  <p>
    Two blocks above name a partial and render it — one <code>.hbs</code>, one
    <code>.md</code>. The third is the guarded case. Guard with the plain property
    (<code>&#123;&#123;#if partial&#125;&#125;</code>) when a missing block is acceptable, and
    let the page fail when it is not: a missing block on a live page is a decision, not an accident.
  </p>
  {{/content}}

{{/extend}}
